{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7utkwstx3ky5vzsznphlodvzzv36werxlbnsbmwylildqayaglua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and the Rust translation needed **no behavioral fixes** — it was already exact.\n\n## What the library is\n\nOne function: `float pow43(int x)` — a 145-entry `f32` lookup table plus quadratic interpolation. `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` compiles a single file with no options, and `Cargo.toml` declares no optional features, so there is **exactly one build configuration** (verified for `--no-default-features`, default, and `--all-features`, in both `dev` and `release`).\n\n## Phase results\n\n| Phase | Artifact | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | `SYMBOLS.md` | C exports 1 symbol (`pow43`); Rust exports the same. `nm -D` diff **empty both ways**; no unresolved non-libc imports. Nothing was left untranslated. |\n| B | `CONFIGS.md` | **21/21 rows pass** — branch A/B/C × `sign ∈ {0,64}` × `frac <0/=0/>0` × `mult ∈ {16,256}` × index extremes, plus ordering, repetition, 8-thread concurrency, and re-`dlopen`. Includes an **exhaustive sweep of all 8 240 defined inputs** (`x ∈ [-16, 8223]`), bit-for-bit via `to_bits()`. |\n| C | `ERRORS.md` | **16/16 rows pass**. Grep proves the C has *no* rejection path at all (no assert/errno/error code/null/length check), so rows are its two range checks plus every input whose unchecked index leaves `g_pow43[0..=144]`: `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `-17`, `8224`, `x=0`, division-by-zero reachability, 3 000 random `i32`. |\n| D | `VERIFICATION.md` | Symbol parity + every feature combo + both profiles, **plus** the differential suite re-run against C built at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os` — all identical. 39 tests, 39 passing. |\n\n## Two findings worth flagging\n\n1. **A trap that had silently invalidated the suite.** For a `cdylib`-only crate, `cargo test` does *not* rebuild the `.so`. My first harness `dlopen`ed a leftover artifact and **passed with deliberately broken Rust**. The harness now builds the `cdylib` itself (into a private target dir, so it can't deadlock with the enclosing `cargo test`) and asserts the artifact is newer than every file in `src/`.\n2. **Mutation-proven sensitivity.** I injected 21 mutations into `src/lib.rs`; **19 were caught**, and I proved the 2 survivors are *semantically equivalent*, not gaps: `81.000001f32` rounds to the same `f32` as `81.0`, and `x < 129 → x < 128` only affects `x=128`, where `16 * g_pow43[32] == g_pow43[144]` bit-for-bit (`0x44214518`).\n\n## One honest limitation\n\nFor `x < -16` or `x > 8223` the **C itself** reads out of bounds, so its result is a property of gcc's `.rodata` layout, not of the source (e.g. it returns gcc's spilled `2.f/9` literal for `x=8224`). I reproduced the read *structurally* rather than emulating those bytes — faking them would be fabricating behavior. Instead, `err16` proves the divergence region is *exactly* the out-of-table region: scanning `x ∈ [-256, 8500]`, **zero in-domain inputs diverge**, and far-out inputs (`INT_MAX`/`INT_MIN`) fault identically in both images, checked out-of-process so a `SIGSEGV` can't hide.\n\nRun it all with `./verify.sh all` (enumerates feature combos mechanically from `Cargo.toml`, so it stays correct if features are added later)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":478,"cache_read_input_tokens":133369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":478,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89abdd36-4b93-407b-b420-8213123b136a","uuid":"a10dbf7f-0e33-4fb0-876f-eaf152326ec7","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:22:51.363Z"}
